\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Signer-disjoint five-fold protocol (SD-5). (a) Fold assignment for Slovo: six signers with at least 500 videos are always in the training data; the other 188 signers form five groups, each used once as the test set, and 10\% of the signers of the other groups form the validation set. (b) Decision rule: a model is called better or worse only if the 95\% bootstrap confidence interval of the paired difference over test signers excludes zero (illustrative distributions).}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig2_protocol}{{2}{5}{Signer-disjoint five-fold protocol (SD-5). (a) Fold assignment for Slovo: six signers with at least 500 videos are always in the training data; the other 188 signers form five groups, each used once as the test set, and 10\% of the signers of the other groups form the validation set. (b) Decision rule: a model is called better or worse only if the 95\% bootstrap confidence interval of the paired difference over test signers excludes zero (illustrative distributions)}{figure.2}{}}
